@k.alpha-contract:K{ap=[transparent_sprites_75353d50,glows_19e4066b,sprite_atlases_07b42f1f];ck=[~75:Binary-alpha assets contain only 0 and 255 unless an exception is declared.,~56:Composited fixtures agree with the declared alpha model.];nm=~38:Declare alpha and compositing behavior;op=[~55:Keep alpha policy separate from RGB palette membership.,~84:Use the chosen compositing equation consistently through export, import and display.,~73:Inspect edges against light and dark backgrounds after round-trip import.];pc=[@e.alpha-contract];rk=[~78:Fully transparent RGB channels can differ without changing visible appearance.,~59:Multiplying premultiplied RGB by alpha again darkens edges.];rq=[~78:RGBA interpretation, straight or premultiplied alpha, and allowed alpha levels];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0d4c84c1f64ae48044b9,@sbecd5d040a6c73c7d34f,@s7a5659883ebbb47af40d,@sd0675d9c7db2d15689ca,@s1df5f09ac5030214d9ae];tg=[~14:alpha-contract]}
@k.animation-anchors:K{ap=[walk_cycles_e3b8ebff,idle_loops_012679ae,weapon_actions_62ab60be];ck=[~70:Required planted contacts remain fixed through their contact interval.,~71:The loop boundary obeys the same motion policy as internal transitions.];nm=~38:Track contacts and review loop closure;op=[~79:Track contact-point coordinates independently from each frame's crop rectangle.,~90:Use onion-skin or difference views to compare adjacent poses and last-to-first transition.,~78:Permit displacement where the action demands it; lock only specified contacts.];pc=[@e.animation-anchors];rk=[~91:A moving root can coexist with a visually planted foot only after world-space compensation.,~67:A low pixel-difference score does not prove a convincing animation.];rq=[~57:Named anchors, ground line and expected contact intervals];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0d4c84c1f64ae48044b9,@sbecd5d040a6c73c7d34f,@s6f9fa2b06515984fcc7d,@s8682999509ca423faf7b];tg=[~17:animation-anchors]}
@k.asset-provenance:K{ap=[reference_derived_assets_3b7d9e7b,legacy_snippets_5a32b20c,variant_libraries_90013dce];ck=[~72:Every reused external component has its source and reuse basis recorded.,~66:Adaptations identify which parts were reused, redrawn or excluded.];nm=~55:Carry source and adaptation intent into reusable assets;op=[~78:Preserve the original material and record the exact excerpt used as reference.,~77:Separate original creative examples from third-party imagery, fonts and code.,~137:Record reuse permission evidence when distributing sourced material; if it is absent, author an original asset from the functional brief.];pc=[@e.asset-provenance];rk=[~66:An inspiration URL or a copied snippet is not a license statement.,~85:Legacy Waylight colors and UI mandates are project-specific, not universal art rules.];rq=[~88:Original source path, creator information if supplied, intended use and adaptation scope];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0d4c84c1f64ae48044b9,@sbecd5d040a6c73c7d34f,@s09e7d67cd2c4c5501161,@scab252d96f5adc63a1ba,@se21c4eae42870d7c0fcc,@sae84832011e9276ba644];tg=[~16:asset-provenance]}
@k.atlas-reuse-budget:K{ap=[large_modular_actors_75f8c128,sprite_libraries_dab972f8,reused_animation_states_0b96ced6];ck=[~45:Source rectangles reconstruct original parts.,~95:Performance claims include measured conditions and the relevant format or compression settings.];nm=~53:Atlas compatible parts and measure actual render cost;op=[~59:Deduplicate identical raster states using content identity.,~78:Pack compatible parts with deliberate padding and matching companion channels.,~91:Measure memory, draw calls, texture switches and transform costs on the target integration.];pc=[@e.atlas-reuse-budget];rk=[~109:An atlas does not guarantee one draw call; blending, ordering, shaders and renderer limits can split batches.,~77:Uncompressed byte arithmetic is an estimate, not resident memory measurement.];rq=[~75:Texture formats, atlas bounds, material groups and measured target renderer];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0d4c84c1f64ae48044b9,@sbecd5d040a6c73c7d34f,@sd4a2db96bc7a471221d1,@sd0675d9c7db2d15689ca];tg=[~18:atlas-reuse-budget]}
@k.cell-materials:K{ap=[falling_sand_aa7d9365,destructible_materials_8be0910c,cellular_worlds_1b5de0a4];ck=[~49:Every nonempty cell resolves to a known material.,~69:Palette changes cannot change physics merely by changing visible RGB.];nm=~59:Use shared material definitions with per-cell mutable state;op=[~66:Put immutable density or phase thresholds in material definitions.,~90:Store occupancy, temperature, lifetime and ownership only where the simulation needs them.,~98:Derive appearance from material and state without conflating render colors with material identity.];pc=[@e.cell-materials];rk=[~88:The shared-table layout is a proposed architecture, not a confirmed Noita memory layout.,~46:Decorative dust may need only a visual effect.];rq=[~55:Material IDs, behavior table and declared mutable state];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0d4c84c1f64ae48044b9,@sbecd5d040a6c73c7d34f,@see13adde441895964969,@s7cc3ff6196c0168fa0aa];tg=[~14:cell-materials]}
@k.cluster-handoff:K{ap=[tiny_highlights_75f843c3,eyes_d8fe183f,one_pixel_feature_motion_e0c41a77];ck=[~54:The feature remains connected under the declared rule.,~90:Its centroid moves toward the target and any area change stays inside the declared budget.];nm=~49:Move a feature using a deliberate cluster handoff;op=[~68:Establish the leading pixels before withdrawing the trailing pixels.,~82:For narrow features use approved shade transitions if area growth is unacceptable.,~52:Protect surrounding silhouette and feature identity.];pc=[@e.cluster-handoff];rk=[~70:Temporary widening changes volume and may be wrong for rigid material.,~62:A mechanically valid handoff still needs visual timing review.];rq=[~67:Feature mask, permitted temporary area change and connectivity rule];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0d4c84c1f64ae48044b9,@sbecd5d040a6c73c7d34f,@sb45e6e3751f324bb9423,@s4d7be14781becfcef06b];tg=[~15:cluster-handoff]}
@k.companion-alignment:K{ap=[diffuse_normal_pairs_4bc6fdc1,height_maps_ccec93e4,mask_atlases_a3a4d09f,animated_lighting_b38861e4];ck=[~97:Dimensions, original sizes, trim offsets, pivots and frame IDs agree where shared UVs require it.,~72:A channel sampled at a diffuse feature corresponds to that same feature.];nm=~39:Keep all sampled asset channels aligned;op=[~74:Apply the same crop, packing and frame ordering to corresponding channels.,~47:Represent missing optional channels explicitly.,~79:Use recognizable calibration marks to check sample correspondence after import.];pc=[@e.companion-alignment];rk=[~46:Equal dimensions alone do not prove alignment.,~103:Independently packed textures can be valid only when the renderer has an explicit mapping between them.];rq=[~67:Shared canvas, frame IDs, trim offsets, pivots and atlas rectangles];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0d4c84c1f64ae48044b9,@sbecd5d040a6c73c7d34f,@sd0675d9c7db2d15689ca,@sed375025480c499dd0b8];tg=[~19:companion-alignment]}
@k.composed-animation:K{ap=[boss_animation_8b678ba8,weapon_actions_during_locomotion_47e9c9d8,damage_variants_a3339652];ck=[~60:Every animated property has an unambiguous composition rule.,~52:Changing one channel does not reset unrelated state.];nm=~58:Compose independent motion channels with defined ownership;op=[~78:Assign locomotion, aim, recoil, damage and secondary motion to named channels.,~76:Define override or additive behavior when channels affect the same property.,~93:Keep attachment swaps independent of unrelated loop phase unless the action requires a reset.];pc=[@e.composed-animation];rk=[~71:Independent clips still require coordination for contacts and overlaps.,~85:Conflicting channel writes create order-dependent results unless resolved explicitly.];rq=[~56:Channel priorities, affected properties and event inputs];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0d4c84c1f64ae48044b9,@sbecd5d040a6c73c7d34f,@s90c9d5bca62d2ba04d08];tg=[~18:composed-animation]}
@k.continuous-state-final-snap:K{ap=[pixel_rigs_a03d93a4,camera_motion_b83bcf1a,procedural_recoil_2ef0ed6a];ck=[~59:Rendering does not overwrite simulation or animation state.,~71:Final positions align to the declared grid with bounded rounding error.];nm=~55:Keep continuous motion and quantize its final placement;op=[~54:Evaluate continuous parent and child transforms first.,~82:Apply camera transformation before the declared screen-grid quantization boundary.,~46:Retain unsnapped state for subsequent updates.];pc=[@e.continuous-state-final-snap];rk=[~49:Snapping every bone independently can open seams.,~77:Tie rounding differs across languages; specify it for deterministic fixtures.];rq=[~77:Floating-point state, logical scale, camera transform and rounding tie policy];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0d4c84c1f64ae48044b9,@sbecd5d040a6c73c7d34f,@sdeadf11a6b5600c10cce,@s30022ebf5fcdf227e81b];tg=[~27:continuous-state-final-snap]}
@k.coverage-candidates:K{ap=[subpixel_translation_a94e1ea2,candidate_in_betweens_1c4ef46b];ck=[~45:Zero shift reconstructs the source occupancy.,~95:Translation preserves total coverage before clipping and output dimensions remain logical size.];nm=~55:Generate constrained supersampled in-between candidates;op=[~48:Replicate occupancy to a 4x or 8x coverage grid.,~108:Apply integer shifts in that grid, average coverage back to logical cells, and quantize to an approved ramp.,~74:Run feature, palette and silhouette checks before any artistic acceptance.];pc=[@e.coverage-candidates];rk=[~75:Supersampling produces candidates; it is not proof of a hand-authored look.,~89:Clipping at canvas bounds must be explicit; ramp quantization can change apparent volume.];rq=[~81:Integer scale factor, source occupancy, approved coverage ramp and cleanup policy];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0d4c84c1f64ae48044b9,@sbecd5d040a6c73c7d34f,@s2c43d7f2f54d3ffc91de];tg=[~19:coverage-candidates]}
@k.crop-and-anchor:K{ap=[background_removal_6fcdd33a,sprite_extraction_61fea8aa,trimmed_animation_frames_cdbcb207];ck=[~55:Restored pixels and anchors match the untrimmed source.,~84:No intentionally translucent edge is discarded without an explicit threshold policy.];nm=~57:Trim transparent padding while preserving logical anchors;op=[~74:Find the permitted opaque bounds and record trim offset and original size.,~58:Translate pivot and socket coordinates by the crop origin.,~84:Keep restoration metadata so each frame can be reconstructed on its original canvas.];pc=[@e.crop-and-anchor];rk=[~73:A tighter image rectangle can move the sprite if its trim offset is lost.,~106:Removing a background requires an actual mask decision, not blindly treating one RGB color as transparent.];rq=[~75:Original canvas, alpha policy and an anchor in original logical coordinates];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0d4c84c1f64ae48044b9,@sbecd5d040a6c73c7d34f,@se21c4eae42870d7c0fcc,@s6f9fa2b06515984fcc7d,@sd0675d9c7db2d15689ca];tg=[~15:crop-and-anchor]}
@k.destruction-topology:K{ap=[destructible_structures_7edc2652,cell_to_body_conversion_abcf4b6d];ck=[~66:Component union equals the remaining occupancy with no duplicates.,~69:Every occupied cell has exactly one owner at the conversion boundary.];nm=~62:Extract components and preserve occupancy at solver boundaries;op=[~52:Identify connected occupied components after damage.,~109:Extract boundaries with an explicit treatment of diagonal ambiguity, then simplify within gameplay tolerance.,~66:Transfer ownership once and retain a mapping back to source cells.];pc=[@e.destruction-topology];rk=[~69:Component extraction alone does not prove stable rigid-body behavior.,~101:Contour simplification and rerasterization can alter collision shape; measure their error explicitly.];rq=[~88:Connectivity convention, ownership transfer, contour policy and simplification tolerance];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0d4c84c1f64ae48044b9,@sbecd5d040a6c73c7d34f,@s5ceeb8f17fc8a17c4c82,@sd098695f689fce277d9f];tg=[~20:destruction-topology]}
@k.deterministic-cell-update:K{ap=[falling_sand_aa7d9365,liquid_rules_90bc72e8,replayable_cellular_simulation_cba919a0];ck=[~66:Material count is conserved for nonreactive closed-world movement.,~99:No material entity exceeds its per-tick displacement bound; repeated runs with the same seed match.];nm=~44:Bound movement and prevent duplicate updates;op=[~47:Process gravity rules in a declared scan order.,~95:Carry update identity with moving material so it cannot move twice unintentionally in one tick.,~72:Resolve target conflicts deterministically and record boundary behavior.];pc=[@e.deterministic-cell-update];rk=[~70:Bottom-up order alone does not prevent all cross-chunk double updates.,~80:Deterministic ties do not make different algorithms or update orders equivalent.];rq=[~78:Tick identifiers, movement bounds, seeded tie-breaking and conflict resolution];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0d4c84c1f64ae48044b9,@sbecd5d040a6c73c7d34f,@s7949dea4705111b5c020,@s0954f75b8a337ae87533];tg=[~25:deterministic-cell-update]}
@k.dirty-region-wakeup:K{ap=[large_mostly_static_cellular_worlds_f9c5ba14];ck=[~77:Optimized and full-scan outputs agree for the same declared update semantics.,~58:Boundary activity wakes every region that can be affected.];nm=~48:Track active regions using rule influence bounds;op=[~66:Dirty both source and destination neighborhoods when cells change.,~67:Expand the dirty region by the complete next-step influence radius.,~70:Sleep stable regions and wake neighboring chunks for boundary changes.];pc=[@e.dirty-region-wakeup];rk=[~69:64x64 is a source case-study choice, not a universal best chunk size.,~103:Counting fewer cell visits demonstrates less scanning, not automatically faster wall-clock performance.];rq=[~94:Chunk size, complete read/write radius, cross-boundary wake rules and reference full-scan mode];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0d4c84c1f64ae48044b9,@sbecd5d040a6c73c7d34f,@sbcf2514330d38618dbda];tg=[~19:dirty-region-wakeup]}
@k.dither-coverage:K{ap=[limited_palette_gradients_bd5b950c,intentional_texture_255b0db4,ordered_translucency_cca3fe72];ck=[~66:Coverage is the actual selected-cell count divided by total cells.,~50:The pattern changes only within its semantic mask.];nm=~46:Count dither coverage and constrain its region;op=[~72:Use the 4x4 rank matrix [[0,8,2,10],[12,4,14,6],[3,11,1,9],[15,7,13,5]].,~68:For fraction q, select cells with rank < 16*q when 16*q is integral.,~96:Keep the pattern phase consistent across adjacent regions unless a discontinuity is intentional.];pc=[@e.dither-coverage];rk=[~80:The local source's example percentage labels are incorrect; count cells instead.,~77:Dither can add noise and is optional; flat clusters may suit an asset better.];rq=[~66:A tileable threshold matrix, two approved colors and a region mask];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0d4c84c1f64ae48044b9,@sbecd5d040a6c73c7d34f,@sfb20036157388d615374,@s758edf765faca65a9b3b];tg=[~15:dither-coverage]}
@k.dither-phase-motion:K{ap=[water_texture_163b558d,energy_fields_9eb7cb3d,controlled_translucency_b3f63777];ck=[~47:Every phase preserves the specified population.,~54:After one period the original pattern returns exactly.];nm=~44:Animate dither phase with an explicit period;op=[~67:Shift the pattern phase deterministically with wrapped coordinates.,~49:Hold coverage constant when changing phase alone.,~84:Keep stable regions untouched and preview the result at its intended scale and rate.];pc=[@e.dither-phase-motion];rk=[~46:Unseeded per-frame noise causes temporal boil.,~102:Constant coverage and perfect looping do not prove that flicker is comfortable or artistically useful.];rq=[~70:A fixed threshold matrix, motion direction, region and positive period];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0d4c84c1f64ae48044b9,@sbecd5d040a6c73c7d34f,@sfb20036157388d615374,@s11ca30e7b7792778299a];tg=[~19:dither-phase-motion]}
@k.edge-color-migration:K{ap=[slow_movement_73712330,small_contours_0ad9a50f,subpixel_animation_candidates_21643862];ck=[~59:Intermediate frames stay in the palette and feature region.,~57:The chosen motion metric moves in the intended direction.];nm=~50:Encode fractional edge motion with approved colors;op=[~87:Construct coverage changes for the selected edge while keeping output on integer cells.,~38:Map coverage to approved ramp entries.,~96:Measure a luminance- or coverage-weighted centroid and inspect the motion at authored durations.];pc=[@e.edge-color-migration];rk=[~59:Apparent motion depends on contrast and viewing conditions.,~80:This method does not place a physical sprite at a fractional logical coordinate.];rq=[~52:Known background, edge ramp and an edge feature mask];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0d4c84c1f64ae48044b9,@sbecd5d040a6c73c7d34f,@s13506aa304092b45e0b3,@secd4065347ec61d027e6];tg=[~20:edge-color-migration]}
