@k.frame-timing:K{ap=[sprite_animation_9537e27d,attacks_ced7c095,idle_loops_012679ae,ui_feedback_adf3d2c9];ck=[~85:Every duration is positive and playback reaches the expected frame at boundary times.,~64:One-shot terminal states and looping wrap behavior are explicit.];nm=~45:Author duration and event semantics per frame;op=[~60:Store durations explicitly rather than assuming uniform FPS.,~67:Name anticipation, action, impact and settle events where relevant.,~80:Define half-open time intervals so event and frame boundaries have no ambiguity.];pc=[@e.frame-timing];rk=[~63:More frames do not automatically improve weight or readability.,~62:Unspecified preview FPS must not overwrite authored durations.];rq=[~65:Ordered frame IDs, positive durations and loop or one-shot policy];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0d4c84c1f64ae48044b9,@sbecd5d040a6c73c7d34f,@s2b7b40856e5ec960ea14,@sb09f91a3c2434f03bc07];tg=[~12:frame-timing]}
@k.integer-presentation:K{ap=[strict_grid_games_a7cd2a47,pixel_previews_014b1177,sprite_delivery_638f99a7];ck=[~75:A logical pixel expands into a uniform scale-by-scale block in the fixture.,~64:No new colors appear during opaque nearest-neighbor enlargement.];nm=~59:Render at a declared logical grid and inspect device pixels;op=[~87:Render or sample at the logical grid, then use a declared integer scale where required.,~83:Apply nearest sampling to image scaling and account for browser device pixel ratio.,~68:Inspect the final output, not only a CSS property or import setting.];pc=[@e.integer-presentation];rk=[~63:Nearest filtering alone does not constrain lighting resolution.,~90:Noninteger scaling, arbitrary rotation and browser zoom can change displayed pixel widths.];rq=[~68:Logical resolution, camera convention and target viewport dimensions];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0d4c84c1f64ae48044b9,@sbecd5d040a6c73c7d34f,@s54972c78922906eca1d4,@s4990356756a7c6f0db61,@s30022ebf5fcdf227e81b];tg=[~20:integer-presentation]}
@k.material-channel-budget:K{ap=[a_2_5d_assets_abb1ddf4,lamps_dfe0b81f,lava_5ed45566,material_effects_cb439ae4];ck=[~68:Every declared channel has a named consumer and documented fallback.,~79:Response-mask zero suppresses the masked term; emission follows its own policy.];nm=~58:Add height, masks and emission only with defined consumers;op=[~67:Keep color, direction, height, response mask and emission distinct.,~65:Declare packing and whether values are color data or linear data.,~97:Reject unsupported channels at integration rather than silently treating them as active features.];pc=[@e.material-channel-budget];rk=[~67:Extra channels increase authoring, memory and synchronization work.,~91:An image generator returning a map does not establish that an engine consumes it correctly.];rq=[~79:Per-channel meaning, numeric range, coordinate convention and renderer consumer];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0d4c84c1f64ae48044b9,@sbecd5d040a6c73c7d34f,@s7a5659883ebbb47af40d,@s5b94c11b6d19fd02dc7d,@s1d98dd6a89c81ed0cb72];tg=[~23:material-channel-budget]}
@k.material-ramps:K{ap=[recoloring_7ad2d6ee,shaded_sprites_331bace0,palette_lighting_28f9e4d9];ck=[~47:Ramp lookup never escapes its assigned palette.,~64:A recolor preserves the declared ordering and region membership.];nm=~41:Use material-specific value and hue ramps;op=[~63:Build dark-to-light ramps appropriate to the material and mood.,~70:Assign each material's pixels to its ramp and retain semantic indices.,~99:Use hue shifts only where the art direction calls for them; inspect neighboring materials together.];pc=[@e.material-ramps];rk=[~102:Hue shifting and monotonically increasing numerical luminance are choices, not universal requirements.,~70:Different materials may intentionally share colors or intersect ramps.];rq=[~55:Named material regions and approved ordered color ramps];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0d4c84c1f64ae48044b9,@sbecd5d040a6c73c7d34f,@s85bd050974b760935077,@s2ee86f3628fad9082734];tg=[~14:material-ramps]}
@k.normal-direction:K{ap=[normal_mapped_sprites_7bf74c92,a_2_5d_surfaces_67ade9c2];ck=[~60:Decoded vectors are finite and unit length within tolerance.,~79:A right-facing slope responds more strongly to right-side than left-side light.];nm=~51:Validate normal encoding and coordinate orientation;op=[~70:Treat normal channels as direction data under the importer convention.,~68:Decode and normalize with a defined fallback for degenerate vectors.,~79:Use a directional fixture to validate handedness and green-channel orientation.];pc=[@e.normal-direction];rk=[~66:Applying an sRGB transfer curve to normal data changes directions.,~79:An 8-bit flat normal is approximate; compare with quantization-aware tolerance.];rq=[~74:Normal axis convention, color-space interpretation and unit-vector decoder];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0d4c84c1f64ae48044b9,@sbecd5d040a6c73c7d34f,@s865bd1ba2a17d94b2f3d,@s0a4ea12376200e71ced8];tg=[~16:normal-direction]}
@k.palette-contract:K{ap=[indexed_sprites_40eaa310,limited_palette_styles_c8701d42,material_ramps_1ca01010];ck=[~45:Every checked pixel maps to an allowed index.,~64:Palette changes retain stable semantic meaning and transparency.];nm=~37:Declare and validate a scoped palette;op=[~75:Assign stable palette indices and reserve any transparent entry explicitly.,~96:Validate opaque pixels against the palette; keep lighting-output exemptions separately declared.,~85:Apply color replacements by semantic ramp rather than unrestricted RGB interpolation.];pc=[@e.palette-contract];rk=[~89:A fixed small palette is optional art direction, not a universal definition of pixel art.,~74:RGBA data can be palette-constrained without using an indexed file format.];rq=[~68:An approved RGBA palette, color-space choice and transparency policy];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0d4c84c1f64ae48044b9,@sbecd5d040a6c73c7d34f,@s85bd050974b760935077,@s39d714f1c01244c707bf,@s0dc8f4cffeaaf9841de6];tg=[~16:palette-contract]}
@k.palette-lighting:K{ap=[stylized_dynamic_lighting_03e113af,strict_output_palettes_2c42d882];ck=[~47:Band index remains in 0..K-1 for finite inputs.,~44:Ramp-output mode emits only declared colors.];nm=~59:Quantize light response and optionally select palette ramps;op=[~74:Compute or accept continuous light intensity separately from raster color.,~58:Clamp intensity to the declared range before quantization.,~126:For strict palette output choose a material ramp entry; multiplying RGB by a band does not itself preserve palette membership.];pc=[@e.palette-lighting];rk=[~67:Banding can shimmer as a light moves; inspect temporal transitions.,~52:Lighting quantization is an optional style decision.];rq=[~73:Finite intensity, K>=2 bands, clamping policy and optional material ramps];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0d4c84c1f64ae48044b9,@sbecd5d040a6c73c7d34f,@sbc024886c77e7c05c60b];tg=[~16:palette-lighting]}
@k.phased-write-ownership:K{ap=[parallel_cellular_simulation_a5cf2c2e];ck=[~58:Every concurrent pair has empty write-domain intersection.,~122:A serial execution of the same phase ordering agrees with its parallel implementation when deterministic mode is promised.];nm=~61:Schedule only disjoint writable cellular regions concurrently;op=[~84:Compute each job's possible write domain, including halos and cascaded rule effects.,~48:Group jobs only when these domains are disjoint.,~91:Place required barriers between phases and re-evaluate ownership if movement bounds change.];pc=[@e.phased-write-ownership];rk=[~70:Copying four phases is unsafe when a different rule can write farther.,~90:Rectangular halo estimates may be conservative; smaller shapes need proof, not assumption.];rq=[~67:Exact job write domains, maximum displacement and barrier semantics];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0d4c84c1f64ae48044b9,@sbecd5d040a6c73c7d34f,@s59edb2777f4e156dfa86];tg=[~22:phased-write-ownership]}
@k.pipeline-order:K{ap=[combined_pixel_systems_302f11bb,engine_integration_aa7bd944];ck=[~72:No stage reads data before its producer or ownership transfer completes.,~123:Continuous animation precedes final snapping; quantized lighting precedes final enlargement when that pipeline is selected.];nm=~68:Validate dependency order across simulation, animation and rendering;op=[~131:Name simulation updates, structural conversion, animation evaluation, snapping, lighting and final presentation as separate stages.,~90:Schedule according to actual dependencies and document any engine-specific feedback cycle.,~81:Validate declared stage order and require capabilities for each requested output.];pc=[@e.pipeline-order];rk=[~80:The source sequence is a proposal; engine physics order may legitimately differ.,~58:A metadata declaration is not evidence that any stage ran.];rq=[~52:Stage dependency graph and ownership transfer points];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0d4c84c1f64ae48044b9,@sbecd5d040a6c73c7d34f,@s693c4ab5bb437e85f090,@s5f6b90cf544aa9f77b22];tg=[~14:pipeline-order]}
@k.preserve-authored-shading:K{ap=[hand_shaded_sprites_4c98f64c,hybrid_pixel_lighting_c5cd36d0];ck=[~41:Zero modulation reproduces diffuse input.,~70:Any palette or value clamps are explicit and applied after modulation.];nm=~53:Declare how dynamic light combines with baked shading;op=[~58:Record whether volume already exists in the diffuse image.,~57:Choose dynamic-light modulation appropriate to that mode.,~83:Compare baseline, neutral-light and opposing-light states to detect double shading.];pc=[@e.preserve-authored-shading];rk=[~65:A generated normal map can interpret painted shadows as geometry.,~82:Strong dynamic lighting can contradict highlights already painted into the sprite.];rq=[~76:Authored-shade, flat-albedo or hybrid mode and a bounded modulation strength];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0d4c84c1f64ae48044b9,@sbecd5d040a6c73c7d34f,@s324320c0bc6fdf2eeea4,@s7a5659883ebbb47af40d];tg=[~25:preserve-authored-shading]}
@k.reaction-tables:K{ap=[thermal_worlds_f25125a8,material_chemistry_e8c9b182,emergent_effects_0e1fd681];ck=[~60:Unknown materials and invalid probabilities fail validation.,~59:Reaction outcomes occur only when declared conditions hold.];nm=~41:Encode material reactions as bounded data;op=[~61:Separate immutable reaction definitions from live cell state.,~91:Validate references, probability ranges, temperature conditions and available output space.,~73:Define reaction priority and accounting rules before combining reactions.];pc=[@e.reaction-tables];rk=[~97:Gameplay chemistry need not conserve real chemical mass, but its own accounting must be explicit.,~68:Different reaction order can change results even with the same seed.];rq=[~87:Known reactants, conditions, output materials, probability policy and conflict ordering];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0d4c84c1f64ae48044b9,@sbecd5d040a6c73c7d34f,@s096eae2d738b6b4b4979,@s7cc3ff6196c0168fa0aa];tg=[~15:reaction-tables]}
@k.representation-owner:K{ap=[all_asset_briefs_60e49b74];ck=[~76:Every requested behavior has an owner and an explicit input/output contract.,~90:A decorative effect does not acquire physical simulation merely because it looks granular.];nm=~49:Choose the representation that owns each behavior;op=[~154:Classify independently moving matter as cells, shape-preserving parts as attachments, pose-dependent topology as frames, and surface response as channels.,~85:Record multiple owners when one asset spans systems and name the conversion boundary.];pc=[@e.representation-owner];rk=[~101:This classification recommends an architecture; it does not make PixelLab or a renderer implement it.,~51:A single asset may require several representations.];rq=[~64:A brief naming visual, physical, animation and lighting behavior];so=[@s9607720391d7364f4ce0,@s0d4c84c1f64ae48044b9,@sbecd5d040a6c73c7d34f,@sd14879708c15da8da087,@s0ce50522100ce64c2c74,@s5f6b90cf544aa9f77b22];tg=[~20:representation-owner]}
